<exercisegroup cols="2">
<title>Isolating via matrix algebra</title>

<introduction><p>
	In each case,
	use matrix algebra to isolate and determine the unknown variable matrix.
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle
		\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
			-8 \amp  7 \\
			 0 \amp -3
		\end{abmatrix}
		- 2 X
		=
		\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
			 5 \amp 0 \\
			-6 \amp 8
		\end{abmatrix}
	</m></p></statement>

	<solution><p>
		It's less messy to perform algebraic manipulations with letters,
		so assign
		<md><mrow>
			A \amp =
			\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
				-8 \amp  7 \\
				 0 \amp -3
			\end{abmatrix}
			\text{,}
			\amp
			B \amp =
			\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
				5 \amp 0 \\
				-6 \amp 8
			\end{abmatrix}
			\text{.}
		</mrow></md>
		Then we have
		<md alignment="gather">
			<mrow> A - 2 X = B </mrow>
			<mrow> A - B = 2 X </mrow>
			<mrow> X = \tfrac{1}{2} (A - B) </mrow>
		</md>
		and we may calculate
		<md>
			<mrow>
				A - B \amp =
				\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
					-8 \amp  7 \\
					 0 \amp -3
				\end{abmatrix}
				-
				\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
					 5 \amp 0 \\
					-6 \amp 8
				\end{abmatrix}
			</mrow>

			<mrow>
				\amp =
				\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
					-13 \amp   7 \\
					  6 \amp -11
				\end{abmatrix}
			</mrow>

		</md>,
		<md>

			<mrow> X \amp = \tfrac{1}{2} (A - B) </mrow>

			<mrow>
				\amp =
				\frac{1}{2}
				\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
					-13 \amp   7 \\
					  6 \amp -11
				\end{abmatrix}
			</mrow>

			<mrow>
				\amp =
				\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
					-\frac{13}{2} \amp  \frac{ 7}{2} \\
					      3       \amp -\frac{11}{2}
				\end{abmatrix}
			</mrow>

		</md>.
	</p></solution>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle
		5 \utrans{X}
		+
		\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
			-3 \amp -7 \\
			 3 \amp  6 \\
			-1 \amp -1
		\end{abmatrix}
		=
		\zerovec
	</m></p></statement>

	<solution>

		<p>
		It's less messy to perform algebraic manipulations with letters,
		so assign
		<md>
			A =
			\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
				-3 \amp -7 \\
				 3 \amp  6 \\
				-1 \amp -1
			\end{abmatrix}
		</md>.
		Then we have
		<md alignment="gather">
			<mrow> 5 \utrans{X} + A = \zerovec </mrow>
			<mrow> 5 \utrans{X} = - A </mrow>
			<mrow> \utrans{X} = - \tfrac{1}{5} A </mrow>
		</md>.
		The final algebraic step is to <q>undo</q> the transpose that has been applied to <m>X</m>,
		but by <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-transpose-transpose">Rule</xref>
		of <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules" />,
		transpose reverses itself:
		<md>
			<mrow> \utrans{X} = - \tfrac{1}{5} A </mrow>
			<mrow> \utrans{(\utrans{X})} = \utrans{(- \tfrac{1}{5} A)} </mrow>
			<mrow> X = - \tfrac{1}{5} \utrans{A} </mrow>
		</md>,
		where in the last step we have also applied
		<xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-transpose-smul">Rule</xref> of
		<xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules" />.
		</p>

		<p>
		The above algebra now tells us what to calculate:
		<md>

			<mrow>
				\utrans{A} \amp =
				\utrans{\begin{abmatrix}{rr}
					-3 \amp -7 \\
					 3 \amp  6 \\
					-1 \amp -1
				\end{abmatrix}}
			</mrow>

			<mrow>
				\amp =
				\begin{abmatrix}{rrr}
					-3 \amp 3 \amp -1 \\
					-7 \amp 6 \amp -1
				\end{abmatrix}
			</mrow>

		</md>,
		<md>

			<mrow> X \amp = - \tfrac{1}{5} \utrans{A} </mrow>

			<mrow>
				\amp =
				- \frac{1}{5}
				\begin{abmatrix}{rrr}
					-3 \amp 3 \amp -1 \\
					-7 \amp 6 \amp -1
				\end{abmatrix}
			</mrow>

			<mrow>
				\amp =
				\begin{abmatrix}{rrr}
					\frac{3}{5} \amp -\frac{3}{5} \amp \frac{1}{5} \\
					\frac{7}{5} \amp -\frac{6}{5} \amp \frac{1}{5}
				\end{abmatrix}
			</mrow>

		</md>.
		</p>

	</solution>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
